     "text": "Page 14  ##\n**Roman PLC Medical Group**\n\n**Re: Mary Garcia (DOB 06/03/1990)**\n\nOctober 18, 2024\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nThis letter serves to provide a comprehensive medical overview of Ms. Mary Garcia, who has been under my care for the treatment of Alcohol use disorder (treated). As requested, I have outlined her medical history, treatment progress, and relevant clinical data for your review.\n\n**Recent Visit Summary:**\n\nOn October 18, 2024, Ms. Garcia was seen for regarding her Alcohol use disorder, which is currently in a treated state. During this visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 137/91, and her weight was 146 pounds. This visit was continuation of her ongoing treatment plan, which includes outpatient care and participation in Alcoholics Anonymous (AA). It is pertinent to note that Ms. Garcia has been abstinent from alcohol for approximately 3.8 years, despite experiencing one relapse during this period.\n\n**Previous Visits Summary:**\n\n**February 11, 2024**\n\nOn February 11, 2024, Ms. Garcia was seen for continued management of her Alcohol use disorder. Her blood pressure at that time was 142/89, and she weighed 145 pounds. She continues to engage in outpatient treatment and attend AA meetings regularly. As mentioned, she has maintained sobriety for about 3.8 years, with only one documented relapse.\n\n**June 6, 2023**\n\nDuring her visit on 6, Z023, Ms. Garcia's blood pressure was recorded at 134/94, and she weighed 157 pounds. Her treatment plan remains consistent with outpatient care and active participation in AA. Her sobriety duration was noted at approximately 3.8 years, with a single relapse incident.\n\n**September 29, 2022**\n\nOn September 29, 2022, Ms. Garcia was seen for ongoing management of her Alcohol use disorder. Her blood pressure at that time was 139/94, and her weight was 146 pounds. She continues her outpatient treatment and AA involvement. Her duration of abstinence from alcohol was approximately 3.8 years, with a single reported relapse.\n\n**Social History:**\n\nMs. Garcia has a history of tobacco use, having smoked cigarettes at a frequency 1.5 packs per day. She began smoking on February 22, 2010, and successfully quit on July 18, 2023. She has been honest and forthcoming about her tobacco use and cessation efforts.\n\n**Additional Findings:**\n\nThroughout her visits, Ms. Garcia's physical examinations have been largely unremarkable with no major deviations from normal findings. She has reported no other significant health issues or complaints apart from her primary diagnosis of Alcohol use disorder.\n\n**Medication:**\n\nMs. Garcia i"
